<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Husayn ibn Ali</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">killed <a href="/years/680">680 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Husayn ibn Ali was a grandson of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a> and the son of Ali, the fourth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>. He refused to recognise the Umayyad caliph <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazid-i">Yazid I</a> and was killed with his companions at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-karbala">Karbala</a> in 680 CE. His death became a defining event for Shia <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and a lasting challenge to the legitimacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The ta’zieh passion plays commemorating the martyrdom of <b>Imam Hosein</b> flourished, and in 1868 the shah built a royal theatre for them, the Takyeh Dowlat.</blockquote><a href="/empire/qajar-iran">Qajar Iran · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>…nomination of his son Yazid as successor led directly to the Second Fitna (civil war, 680–692), during which <b>Husayn ibn Ali</b>, Ali's son and Muhammad's grandson, was killed with a small band of followers at Karbala in 680 by forces sent by Yazid's governor of Iraq, Ubayd Allah…</blockquote><a href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Abbasid forces crushed an Alid revolt led by al-<b>Husayn ibn Ali</b>, a descendant of Hasan ibn Ali, near Mecca; al-Husayn and many of his followers were killed.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-11">11 June in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Husayn ibn Ali</b>, grandson of the Prophet Muhammad, who had refused to recognise the Umayyad caliph Yazid I, was killed with most of his small band by Yazid's forces at Karbala.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-10">10 October in history</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1705, during an invasion from the Regency of Algiers, the cavalry officer <b>Husayn ibn Ali</b> seized power in Tunis and founded the Husainid dynasty.</blockquote><a href="/state/beylik-of-tunis">Beylik of Tunis</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1702 the Muradid line was destroyed, and in 1705 <b>Husayn ibn Ali</b> seized power, founding the Husainid dynasty of the Beylik of Tunis.</blockquote><a href="/state/ottoman-tunisia">Ottoman Tunisia</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a>. Died in Karbala, in what is now <a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=24.47,39.61&amp;year=680" aria-label="Medina on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5603 1263 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Husayn ibn Ali"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6053 1533h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6053 1533h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=24.47,39.61&amp;year=680">What was here in 680 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
